## Step 2: Identify Pareto Front (maximize both Modulus and Pore Fraction)

A point is non-dominated if no other point has both higher modulus AND higher pore fraction.

Sorting by modulus descending and checking pore fraction:

- **17p5-5deg-550s-N2 run1**: 777.89 / 0.27 — but top gap defect, run2 gave 342.5/0.35 (very different, high CV=0.25, wrinkle). Not reproducible.
- **17p5-10deg-15s-N2 run1**: 708.94 / 0.28 — good quality. Run2: 474.72/0.33. Run3: 515.67/0.28. Large inter-run variability.
- **17p5-20deg-90s-N2 run1**: 683.29 / 0.28 — good quality. Run2 and run3 gave missing/327.37 with 0.32. Variable.
- **18p5-5deg-330s-NoN2**: 667.13 / 0.25 — bubble+wrinkle defects.
- **17p5-15deg-60s-N2 run2**: 695.94 / 0.26 — minor wrinkle, high SD (186.99).
- **17p5-25deg-375s-N2 run1**: 591.67 / 0.28 — good quality. Run2: 419.28/0.33.
- **19p5-25deg-130s-NoN2 run1**: 350.75 / 0.43 — low modulus but highest pore fraction. Run4: 570.22/0.21. Runs 2,3 missing modulus. Very inconsistent.
- **17p5-15deg-60s-N2 run1**: 519.51 / 0.36 — good quality, run2 gave 695.94/0.26.
- **19-10deg-240s-NoN2 run2**: 308.88 / 0.37 — low modulus.
- **18-15deg-600s-NoN2 run1**: 476.82 / 0.39 — top gap defect. Run2: 339.82/0.32.

**Pareto-front candidates** (no point dominates them on both objectives simultaneously, among well-measured points):

1. **17p5-15deg-60s-N2**: run1 gives 519.51/0.36, run2 gives 695.94/0.26 — two independent runs with both objectives measured. The runs are inconsistent (modulus varies 519→696, pore fraction 0.36→0.26). This is a validated candidate but with high variability between runs.

2. **19p5-25deg-130s-NoN2**: run1=350.75/0.43, run4=570.22/0.21. Runs 2 and 3 missing modulus. Highly inconsistent.

3. **17p5-10deg-15s-N2**: run1=708.94/0.28, run2=474.72/0.33, run3=515.67/0.28. Three runs, inconsistent modulus.

## Step 3: Assess Validation Status

**17p5-15deg-60s-N2** (mixing_temp=65, bath_temp=15, pullcast_speed=10, nitrogen=True, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=60, nips_bath_wait_time=1800, polymer_wt=17.5):
- Run1: Modulus=519.51, PF=0.36, good quality
- Run2: Modulus=695.94 (SD=186.99, very high), PF=0.26, minor wrinkle, low coupon humidity (7.79 vs 7.75) — unusual environmental condition (coupon humidity ~8% vs typical ~38-54%)

The run2 coupon humidity of ~7.8% is anomalously low compared to all other experiments (~30-54%). This suggests an unusual drying condition during the N2 blow that may have affected the membrane. The run2 result (695.94/0.26) may not be representative of normal conditions. Run1 (519.51/0.36) was obtained at more typical humidity (~39.75 equivalent... wait, coupon humidity 7.75 for run1 too). Both runs had ~7.75-7.79% coupon humidity — this is a consistent feature of this condition (N2 blow at bath_temp=15°C apparently produces very dry conditions at the coupon stage).

So both runs of 17p5-15deg-60s-N2 had anomalously low coupon humidity. The results differ substantially between runs (modulus 519 vs 696, PF 0.36 vs 0.26). This is high variability.

**Key Pareto-front analysis** (using only good-quality, both-objectives-measured experiments):

Looking for high modulus AND high pore fraction simultaneously:

| Condition | Modulus | PF | Quality |
|---|---|---|---|
| 17p5-15deg-60s-N2 run1 | 519.51 | 0.36 | Good |
| 17p5-15deg-60s-N2 run2 | 695.94 | 0.26 | Minor wrinkle, unusual env |
