## Step 2: Identify Pareto Front (maximize both E and PF)

A point is non-dominated if no other point has both higher E and higher PF.

Sorting by E descending:
- 17p5-15deg-60s-N2 run2: E=696, PF=0.26
- 17p5-10deg-15s-N2 run1: E=709, PF=0.28 — dominates run2 on both
- 17p5-20deg-90s-N2 run1: E=683, PF=0.28 — dominated by run1 (709, 0.28)
- 18p5-5deg-330s-NoN2: E=667, PF=0.25 — dominated by (709, 0.28)
- 17p5-25deg-375s-N2 run1: E=592, PF=0.28 — dominated by (709, 0.28)
- 18-5deg-180s-N2: E=596, PF=0.30 — check: is there anything with E≥596 and PF≥0.30? (709, 0.28) has higher E but lower PF. Not dominated.
- 17-0add-5deg-run2: E=547, PF=0.31 — dominated by (596, 0.30)? No: 596>547 but 0.30<0.31. Not dominated.
- 19p5-5deg-0s-N2: E=567, PF=0.33 — dominated by (596, 0.30)? 596>567 but 0.30<0.33. Not dominated by that. Check (709,0.28): higher E, lower PF. Not dominated.
- 18p5-5deg-105s-N2: E=593, PF=0.33 — dominated by (596, 0.30)? 596>593 but 0.30<0.33. Not dominated. But quality is poor (top gap, wrinkle).
- 19-10deg-240s-NoN2 run1: E=516, PF=0.33 — dominated by (593, 0.33) or (596, 0.30)? (593,0.33): 593>516 and 0.33=0.33 → dominated.
- 17p5-15deg-60s-N2 run1: E=520, PF=0.36 — check: anything with E≥520 and PF≥0.36? (596,0.30): higher E, lower PF. Not dominated.
- 19p5-25deg-130s-NoN2 run1: E=351, PF=0.43 — check: anything with E≥351 and PF≥0.43? (520,0.36): higher E, lower PF. Not dominated.

**Pareto front candidates** (non-dominated, good quality):
1. **(709, 0.28)** — 17p5-10deg-15s-N2 run1 — but run2 gave (475, 0.33), run3 gave (516, 0.28). High variability across runs.
2. **(596, 0.30)** — 18-5deg-180s-N2 — wrinkles noted, single measurement
3. **(567, 0.33)** — 19p5-5deg-0s-N2 — coverage gaps + wrinkles, single measurement
4. **(593, 0.33)** — 18p5-5deg-105s-N2 — top gap, wrinkle, non-uniform; single measurement
