## Step 2: Identify Pareto Front (maximize both E and PF)

A point is non-dominated if no other point has both higher E and higher PF.

Sorting by E descending and checking PF:

- **17p5-5deg-550s-N2-1450s run1**: E=778, PF=0.27 — but top gap defect, run2 gave E=343, PF=0.35 (very inconsistent, high CV=0.25 in run2). Not reproducible.
- **17p5-20deg-90s-N2-1250s run1**: E=683, PF=0.28 — run2 had no objectives measured, run3 gave E=327, PF=0.32. Highly inconsistent.
- **17p5-15deg-60s-N2-1800s run2**: E=696, PF=0.26 — run1 gave E=520, PF=0.36; run3 gave E=407, PF=0.32. Very high variability across runs.
- **18p5-5deg-330s-NoN2-1800s**: E=667, PF=0.25 — single run, bubble+wrinkle defects, only 1 specimen survived fit.
- **17p5-10deg-15s-N2-1800s run1**: E=709, PF=0.28 — run2 gave E=475, PF=0.33; run3 gave E=516, PF=0.28. Inconsistent.
