## Step 4: Identify the Most Promising Unexplored Region

Looking at the data patterns:
- Higher PF (>0.35) tends to occur at: bath_temp=15°C (run1 of 17p5-15deg), bath_temp=25°C with high mixing temp (19p5 run1), bath_temp=10°C with no-N2 (19-10deg run2 PF=0.37)
- Higher E (>600) tends to occur at: lower polymer_wt (~17-17.5), bath_temp=5-10°C, N2=True, moderate wait times

The **17p5-15deg-60s-N2-1800s** condition showed run1 with E=520, PF=0.36 — a genuinely attractive combination (high PF with decent E). However, run3 had a top gap defect and run2 had low PF=0.26. The condition is noisy.

**Key observation**: The condition **17p5-10deg-90s-N2-1800s** (single run) gave E=442, PF=0.31 with good quality. Nearby conditions suggest bath_temp=10°C with polymer_wt=17.5 and N2=True is a productive region.

**What hasn't been tried**: Combining the features that seem to push toward high E (low bath temp, N2, moderate wait) with features that push toward high PF (bath_temp ~10-15°C, moderate wait times). 

Looking at the best confirmed single-run result for balanced objectives: **17-0add-5deg-run2** (E=547, PF=0.31, good quality, CV=0.11) is a solid unvalidated candidate. But more interesting is exploring **polymer_wt=17.5, bath_temp=10°C, N2=True** with a longer wait time to try to push PF higher while maintaining E.

The condition **17p5-10deg-90s-N2-1800s** gave E=442, PF=0.31 with good quality. The **17p5-10deg-15s-N2-1800s** averaged E≈567, PF≈0.30 across 3 runs. 

**New exploration**: Try **polymer_wt=17.5, bath_temp=10°C, N2=True, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=45s** (between 15s and 90s), with mixing_temp=65, pullcast_speed=8, nips_bath_wait_time=1800. This interpolates between two tested points in a region that has shown consistently good quality membranes and moderate-to-good performance on both objectives.

Actually, stepping back: the most important gap is that many high-performing single runs haven't been validated. The **17-0add-5deg-30s-N2-1200s run2** (E=547, PF=0.31, good quality, CV=0.11) is a clean single run worth validating — but it uses polymer_wt=17.0 which is a different condition from the 17.5 cluster.

Given the instruction to prioritize objective improvement in optimize mode while respecting uncertainty, I should explore a new condition that could plausibly improve on the current best confirmed performance. The best reproducible performance across multiple runs is approximately E~550, PF~0.30-0.31.

**Target**: Push PF toward 0.35+ while keeping E above 500. The 17p5-15deg-60s run1 showed this is possible (E=520, PF=0.36) but was noisy. A nearby unexplored point: **polymer_wt=17.5, bath_temp=12°C (not available — only 5,10,15,20,25 are typical)** — bath_temp is continuous so 12°C is valid.

